So if I have an entity like this:

```
@Entity()
@Index(["country","iso3","region","name","pollutant"], { unique: true })
export class ExposureRegion implements Region {

    @PrimaryColumn()
    @Column({ length: 56 })
    country?: string;

    @PrimaryColumn()
    @Column({ length: 6})
    iso3?: string;

    @PrimaryColumn()
    @Column({ length: 12})
    region?: string;

    @PrimaryColumn()
    @Column({ length: 56})
    name?: string;

    @PrimaryColumn()
    @Column({ length: 5})
    pollutant?: string;

}

```

Where the primary key is actually a composite key of all the columns in the table, then there would be no way right now to do a query where you select only one of those columns. Correct?

